Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/mdp5: distinguish exhausted display resources from OOM

Failure to find an unused compatible hardware pipe is a display resource
constraint, not an allocation failure. Return ENOSPC for this case. Also
preserve the SMP allocator's error instead of translating ENOSPC to ENOMEM.
Actual memory-allocation errors from mdp5_get_global_state remain intact.

libliftoff0.5 backs out and tries another allocation for EINVAL, ERANGE or
ENOSPC. ENOMEM aborts its search. On MSM8226 a three-full-width-plane
TEST_ONLY request exceeds the seven SMP blocks, so misreporting this
constraint prevents otherwise valid two-plane allocations being explored.

This does not increase hardware limits or alter register programming.
Device test evidence: docs/GRAPHICS-BOTTLENECK.md.

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/mdp5/mdp5_pipe.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/mdp5/mdp5_pipe.c
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/mdp5/mdp5_pipe.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/mdp5/mdp5_pipe.c
@@ -86,10 +86,10 @@ int mdp5_pipe_assign(struct drm_atomic_commit *s, struct drm_plane *plane,
 	}
 
 	if (!(*hwpipe))
-		return -ENOMEM;
+		return -ENOSPC;
 
 	if (r_hwpipe && !(*r_hwpipe))
-		return -ENOMEM;
+		return -ENOSPC;
 
 	if (mdp5_kms->smp) {
 		int ret;
@@ -101,7 +101,7 @@ int mdp5_pipe_assign(struct drm_atomic_commit *s, struct drm_plane *plane,
 		ret = mdp5_smp_assign(mdp5_kms->smp, &new_global_state->smp,
 				(*hwpipe)->pipe, blkcfg);
 		if (ret)
-			return -ENOMEM;
+			return ret;
 
 		(*hwpipe)->blkcfg = blkcfg;
 	}
